name:Deus, cujus Filius (oratio ad processionem);
office-part:Oratio;
mode:;
book:Processionarium O.P. (Cormier), 1913, pp. 50-51 (text, with its flexa after captívam, colon after nobis, flexa after sæculórum);
commentary:Prayer: Art. III § III, pp. 407-408 ("Modus cantandi Orationes ad Horas, et quotiescumque aliquae aliae Orationes quae non sunt de corpore Officii et Missae cantandae fuerint"), applied after its printed example Concéde nos fámulos tuos (p. 407) and conclusions (p. 408): Orémus h h f, tenor h, at the flexa (the sign after the word in the text of this page) the syllables after the last accent fall to f, at the metrum (colon in the text of this page) the two syllables before the last accent (three if the third ends a dactyl, Art. III § II 2°, p. 405) on g, the last of them on f, the accent and the rest on h, R. Amen g h (p. 401, VII 2°, p. 408). The inflexions fall where this page marks them, not where the site text has its punctuation. F clef on the 3rd line as printed.;
transcriber:the tone of the Processionarium O.P. 1913 applied to this text for this site (the book prints no melody with this text);
